 a bit more challenge than your  typical events already present in the  game for example the first one is  actually at the main hub it's this very  hard obstacle course that needs to be  beaten in three minutes the relics are  weird equipment called funkies i haven't  mentioned this but there is a group of  riders called the shack daddy bandits  they're famous for doing bizarre stunts  with very weird equipment like wing  suiting with a cardboard plane or using  skis made of old wood they also have  their own events and challenges but  regardless they are pretty cool it's  nice to see some bizarre and wacky  equipment you can use in the game  however the 500 balloons are insane  they're not marked on the map and  they'll only give you a small bit of  money you could claim that it's for the  seasoned player who wants to explore  every inch of the map but i think that's  a poor excuse in an attempt to defend  them ubisoft really wants to get away  from their tried and true formula with  this game but not too far apparently as  they need to add some sort of  collectible with an astronomical number  it's like the borgia flags of assassin's  creed it's just flat out boring content  and not worth your time besides the  collectibles you have a large map that  you can ride and traverse but i'm  confused about what this game wants if  this game was mainly focused on  completing events and getting stars then  they succeeded but then it feels like  you're just going through a checklist  and taking off boxes the best part about  any of these games is the ability to  ride for hours you could run the same  course over and over again or just go  down a path and see where it takes you  but if they tried to do that then they  barely succeeded the best places to get  that thrill of riding your snowboard or  bike is the courses the game gives you  they're used in the events so why not  use them in the free roam mode they're  obviously the best places to ride down  this works perfectly with the snow  events as there's a ski lift at the  bottom of most of the courses that'll  take you right back up to the top and  you can continue riding again but for  the bikes there is nothing if you want  to ride the same course you need to go  to the course's start then once you  finish or are satisfied with your run  you have to fast travel to a nearby  location then bike your way over to the  starting line again depending on the  course this fast travel could be  thousands of feet away so you're not  even riding to the course anymore you're  just flying to the course every time you  want to reset i think you can understand  how boring this would get this game  needs some sort of checkpoint system  like how skate 3 implemented where if  you want to reset you can just be sent  back to the checkpoint that you put down  because right now i cannot see myself  constantly teleporting and traveling to  a course which might be longer than the  actual course itself however before you  start the game there is an option called  the zen mode which apparently according  to ubisoft as i asked them through email  is an offline mode for the game so maybe  there's something like that in there or  maybe i'm just trying to cope regardless  the exploration does have some real  potential and certain areas are really  fun to explore but most of the fun i had  was running the same snow course for an  hour straight and while i may be in the  minority when it comes to people  enjoying that kind of gameplay i  definitely can't be alone as an overall  note to writer's republic is a really  good game it has a 60 price tag so you  do with that as you will but from what  i've experienced the game is quite fun  and it's a game i'll definitely be  playing in my spare time whenever i have  limited time before something i can  always just load the game up right  around for 10 to 15 minutes then turn it  off but it's also beneficial for those  who want to play for hours and hours at  a time of course it's always up to you  whether or not you want to buy the game  with that however we have come to the  end of the video let me know what you  think about writer's republic down below  and if you did participate in that trial  week before the game's launch do let me  know what you thought about the game as  well like the video if you enjoyed  subscribe if you're new and as always if  you're a returning viewer i thank you  for coming back  take care everyone  and goodbye  [Music]  you

